# The mesh as a graph, on the node detail.
#
# NEIGHBORINFO_APP is the only thing on the wire that says which nodes hear which. Everything
# else describes one link: hops_away is a count, SNR is the reading of the hop that reached us,
# and a traceroute is one path measured once.
#
# Two groups, and the second is the one worth having. "Neighbours" is what the node itself
# reported. "Heard by" is the reverse - nobody reports it, it exists only as every other node's
# list read backwards - and it is the half that answers "is anything hearing me".

scene demo
tab nodes

# The Nodes list has four rows before its first node - the filter row, the sort row, the Map and
# Waypoints (MESH_UI_NODES_LEAD_ROWS) - so a node's row is its index in the demo roster plus
# four. Echo Repeater is seeds[5] and row 9, Delta Camp is
# seeds[4] and row 8.

# Echo Repeater: hears three, and two of those report hearing it back.
key down 9
key a
key down 34
hold 1600
key b

# Delta Camp: hears nobody, which is what a node off the mesh looks like. B left the cursor on
# Echo's own row, so this is one step back up the list rather than an index into it.
key up 1
key a
key down 21
hold 1600
